## Agents

$agents_table

Harness agents live in `harness/agents/<agent>/` (a harness process). The WDL `agents/`
folder at the workspace root means uber agents and is legacy; do not confuse the two.

## Commands for this workspace

Every command takes `--env $env` (or uses the active workspace).

```
abcd ws status --env $env
abcd stage <agent> --env $env
abcd test-staged <agent> --env $env
abcd release <agent> --env $env
abcd rollback <agent> --env $env
abcd audit drift --env $env
```

## Approval rules

- Work on a branch and push it. Changes reach `$default_branch` only by pull request, reviewed
  by someone else. Never commit to `$default_branch` directly.
- `abcd release` requires the staged commit to be on `$default_branch`.
- A release needs the FDE's or lead's explicit approval, recorded by abcd.
- Browser skills need a member approval token or `--local-approval`.
- Never print or commit secrets. `.env` holds credentials and is never committed.
  Capture bundles (`recording_bundle.json`, `*.har`) never go in git.

## Do not touch

- WDL legacy: `agents/`, `actions/`, `pipelines/`, `lambdas/` keep their own tools
  (`save_wdl_draft.py`, `publish_wdl_action.py`, `rollback_changes.py`).
- The default tier: client workspaces release to the org tier only. Never run `deploy-default`.
- `adopt_profile.json` must not hold `security_params` values; cookies belong in `.env`.
